config BR2_PACKAGE_FONT_NOTO_SYMBOLS2
	bool "font-noto-symbols2"
	help
	  Noto Sans Symbols 2: the Unicode symbol blocks no other
	  shipped font covers, e.g. the media-control triangles
	  (U+23F5, Claude Code's mode line) and Symbols for Legacy
	  Computing (U+1FB00, terminal graphs). Ubuntu ships it in
	  fonts-noto-core.

	  https://github.com/notofonts/symbols
